[h1]Phobos Agriculture[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.15.2

[h2]Performance update[/h2]
Bulk-tank searches and panel refreshes reuse shared helpers. Crop growth, cooking, water, nutrients, power and heat rules are unchanged.
Offline checks accompany this draft. Measured improvement and in-game interaction still await owner feedback. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/performance-audit.md]Audit and optional playtesting checks[/url].

[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

A hot meal is a useful thing to come home to. Grow potatoes and lettuce with Verdemorrow equipment, then cook potato portions in the Hearth-2 galley cooker.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Firstlight-4 shows the crop growing across four trays. All four share one crop cycle.
[*]Grow food lettuce or choose the separate seed crop for replacement planting stock.
[*]Start with manual water and nutrients. Add a W2 and irrigation pipes for up to eight linked racks, then an optional R3 water reserve.
[*]Recover recorded crop nutrients at B2, add makeup salts and use the mixture in W2. Older unrecorded waste remains waste.
[*]Buy equipment and supplies or build machinery at supported tables. Some small supplies also appear in newly generated fridges and crates.
[*]Assign routine planting, supply hauling, harvesting and cooking to eligible crew. Choose an optional alert when a meal or crop is ready.
[*]Buy agricultural water and 500 g nutrient charges through station Bulk supplies. Review each quote before buying.
[/list]

[h2]Operating limits[/h2]
Supplies, output space, cabin conditions and power matter. Growth cycles, yields and simplified chemistry are gameplay choices, not NASA or ESA results. Food lettuce produces no seeds. Drainage treatment loses material and never makes drinking water. Wet Recycler rejects have no fertilizer recipe. Loading pauses water transfer; resume when ready. Split stacked supplies before manual processing; partial charges keep their own contents.

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.29.0 or newer. Shipbreaker C1 control is optional. Optional Ship's Water support is scoped to Valtora's inspected 0.16.1; manual supplies remain available.

This is an unpublished development package. Automated checks do not establish in-game readiness or Unity layout approval. Keep required mods installed for saves using their content. Updating does not refill shops or old loot containers. See the installation guide for current download availability.

[h2]English wording update[/h2]
Controls, warnings and descriptions use clearer language. Equipment identities, saved progress, recipes and gameplay values are unchanged.

[h2]Guides, sources and credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited below. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
NASA plant work and ESA MELiSSA inform the crop and recovery research. Bruce Dunn at Oklahoma State University informs hydroponics; NASA porous-tube research informs root-water delivery; Jay Garland of Bionetics (NASA TM-107557) informs the recovery discussion. The linked research guides distinguish findings from our simplified recipes. Valtora owns Ship's Water; its optional integration does not imply endorsement.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; artwork provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

